    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "<INSTRUCTIONS: Considerations for filling out the data card: Deciding the appropriate resolution for documenting a scientific dataset in a data card can be complex. Data cards may describe single or multiple data files, datasets, or versions. Too granular, and there will be too many data cards; too broad, and details may be lost. Consider the use, audience, and documentation the data card needs to provide to maintain transparency without duplication. Reflect on these relationships to balance clarity, usability, and sustainability.>"
      }
