    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@value": "These fields describe the scale of the dataset, which is important for users to understand the scope and potential resource requirements for using the dataset. record_count and record_unit provide a standardized way to describe the number of primary records, samples, files, or other relevant units in the dataset, which is critical for understanding the dataset's size and complexity. compressed_bytes and uncompressed_bytes provide information about the storage requirements for the dataset, which is important for users to plan"
